From 757f8550ac6be2eac82fc03860aba3153155ca58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: workspace-agent <workspace.vm.agent@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:55:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 35/56] M3 particles: material layers and oriented quad types

The particle shader reuses layers.glsl: colour is the diffuse plus the
emissive layers, alpha is the product of the alpha masks (WhiteoutFlakes
m3_standard.slang), both times the particle colour. Before, only the
diffuse was sampled and its alpha used, so masked and emissive-only
materials drew as solid squares.

Quads follow the particle type (WhiteoutFlakes BuildQuad): tail and trail
stretch along the current velocity by max(tail, speed x tail), or the tail
alone with fixLengthTailParts; pinned spans birth point to particle;
terrain lies flat; emitter-oriented uses the emitter axes. Other types
stay billboards. particleQuad is on the m3 cache for the tests.

Known defects: terrain quads ignore instanceAngle (not parsed); types 2,
3, 4, 6 and 8 draw as billboards; world-space emitter-oriented quads use
the emitter axes now, not at birth; every UV source reads the flipbook cell.
